    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναλογ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be analogous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπλάγχνον οὐκ ἔχει ἀναλογοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					334
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.278
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τεχνίτης ὁ -ῶν τῷ Φειδίᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					<u>Nat.Fac.</u>
					2.3
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὴν ἐπιμέλειαν</span>
			<i>to be capable of performing</i> a service, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PAmh.</u>
				64.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῖς τᾶς ἀξίας βάσμοις</span>
			<i>to keep up</i> to the degrees of his rank, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).243.17
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Mytilene</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3486
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thyatira</span>), <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				4.8.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.80c
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Math.,
				<i>to be proportionate,</i>
